.TH hpcscalpel3 "1" "" "The scalpel3 HPC Launcher" "The scalpel3 HPC Launcher"

.SH NAME
hpcscalpel3 \- HPC wrapper for distributed scalpel3 execution

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hpcscalpel3
[\fB-J\fR \fIstart_block\fR]
[\fB-K\fR \fIend_block\fR]
[\fB-A\fR \fIalgorithm\fR]
[\fB-D\fR \fInum_nodes\fR]
[\fB-P\fR]
[\fB-Q\fR \fIblocksize\fR]
[\fB-X\fR]
\fIimgfilename\fR
\fIblockmapfilename\fR
\fB--scalpel\fR
[\fIscalpel options\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBhpcscalpel3\fR is a high-performance computing wrapper that partitions
a disk image into windows and launches multiple \fBscalpel3\fR(1) instances
across distributed nodes.  Each instance processes a portion of the image,
and results are merged afterward.
.PP
All options after \fB--scalpel\fR are passed directly to the underlying
\fBscalpel3\fR instance.

.SH OPTIONS
.PP
.TP
.BI -J " start_block"
Start block for the carve window.
.TP
.BI -K " end_block"
End block for the carve window.
.TP
.BI -A " algorithm"
Windowing algorithm for partitioning the image.
.TP
.BI -D " num_nodes"
Number of distributed processes.
.TP
.B -P
Auto-determine the number of processes.
.TP
.BI -Q " blocksize"
Blocksize in bytes (must be divisible by 512).
.TP
.B -X
Enable debug output.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR scalpel3 (1),
.BR mergeblockmap (1),
.BR mergecps (1)

.SH AUTHOR
Golden G. Richard III.
